---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import LF from "../../components/LF.astro"
import S from "../../components/S.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import astro_ext from "../../img/web/vsc-ext-astro.jpg"
---
<Slide t1="Starting with Astro" splash={ true } t2="What is Astro?">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <LF><S t="orange">Static site generator</S>: completely fixed page content from
            server, rendered ahead of time (cf. PHP (&#129326;))</LF>
            <ul><li class="fragment">No back-end support needed</li></ul>
        <LF><S t="orange">Component based</S>: modular approach to construction of pages</LF>
        <LF><S t="orange">Collections</S>: can assemble tables, sets of pages from data sources</LF>
        <LF><S t="orange">Integrations</S>: supports CSS libraries, frameworks like React, ...</LF>
        <li class="fragment">Open Source</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Installation: Node.js">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li>Command line installation (use a terminal program)</li>
        <li>Astro runs on top of Node.js</li>
        <li>Install using <code>npm</code> command (Node Package Manager)</li>
        <li>Install Node.js (and NPM) from here:
            <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/download/">https://nodejs.org/en/download/</a></li>
        <li>(on macOS: recommend Homebrew, <a href="https://brew.sh/">https://brew.sh/</a>
            for installing NPM and Node.js: <code>brew install nodejs</code>)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Installation: Astro">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li>Command-line install: <code>npm create astro@latest</code></li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide>
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="text" height="550px">
            { "  " + `
  astro   Launch sequence initiated.

    dir   Where should we create your new project?
            ./ossified-osiris

   tmpl   How would you like to start your new project?
            A basic, minimal starter

   deps   Install dependencies?
            Yes

    git   Initialize a new git repository?
            Yes

        ✔  Project initialized!
            ■ Template copied
            ■ Dependencies installed
            ■ Git initialized

   next   Liftoff confirmed. Explore your project!

          Enter your project directory using cd ./ossified-osiris 
          Run npm run dev to start the dev server. CTRL+C to stop.
          Add frameworks like react or tailwind using astro add.

          Stuck? Join us at https://astro.build/chat

 ╭─────╮  Houston:
 │ ◠ ◡ ◠  Good luck out there, astronaut! 🚀
 ╰─────╯`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Run Astro">
    <ul>
        <li><code>cd <em>[project-folder]</em></code></li>
        <li><code>npm run dev</code></li>
        <li>Web server runs at <code>http://localhost:4321</code></li>
        <li class="fragment">Note: this is a <em>development server</em> with browser
            support for hot reloading&mdash;production builds are separate</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Visual Studio Code">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">Recommended: good editor with highlighting, auto-completion etc.
            for Astro pages and components, Markdown, JavaScript, JSX</li>
        <li class="fragment">VS Code support (official)&mdash;highly recommended:</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center fragment">
        <Image
            src={ astro_ext }
            alt="Astro Extension"
            height="300"
            width="500" />
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">Do an <code>Open Folder...</code> on your Astro project</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Astro: First Look">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment"><em>Components</em> (including page layouts): look rather like HTML elements</li>
        <li class="fragment">Components can be parameterised, reused, ...</li>
        <li class="fragment">Components can contain JavaScript code (e.g. for
            collections)&mdash;build time only! (cf. React components)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Experiment">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Open the Astro project folder in VS Code</li>
        <li class="fragment">Start the Astro server: <code>npm run dev</code></li>
        <li class="fragment">edit <code>index.astro</code> and see
            how the page updates immediately</li>
        <li class="fragment">Do the components make sense?</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>
